    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d449">

                <pb facs="0596" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg484"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/7515: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Second Secretary of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-12-12T13:00:00+08:00">December 12, 1935—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 12—11:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>137. 1. The Government is reported to have issued late last night a mandate
                    making the following as members of the Hopei-Chahar Political Affairs
                    Commission: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Sung Cheh-yuan (Chairman); Wan Fu-lin; Wang I-tang; Liu Che; Li Ting-yu;
                            Chia Teh-yao; Hu Yu-kun; Kao Ling-wei; Wang <pb facs="0597" n="485"
                                xml:id="pg485"/> Keh-min; Hsiao Chen-ying; Chin Teh-chun; Chang
                            Tze-chung; Cheng Ke; Chow Tso-min; Men Chih-chung; Shih Ching-ting; Leng
                            Chia-chi.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>2. The regulations governing the Commission are not yet known.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
